 {i:15,ru:'Организаторам пришлось справляться с нехваткой волонтеров.',en:'The organizers had to contend with a shortage of volunteers.',note:'Contend with means deal with a difficulty or opponent.',re:'contend with'},
 {i:16,ru:'Два комитета выясняли отношения из-за бюджета.',en:'The two committees fought it out over the budget.',note:'It is fixed in fight it out. Over introduces the subject of the dispute.',re:'fought it out|fight it out'},
 {i:17,ru:'Менеджер попытался расколоть команду, чтобы управлять ей проще.',en:'The manager tried to divide and conquer the team.',note:'The fixed order is divide and conquer, with conquer in its base form after to.',re:'divide and conquer'},
 {i:18,ru:'Нам нужна передышка, чтобы всё обдумать.',en:'We need to gain some breathing space to think it over.',note:'Breathing space means time or room to think and recover, not physical air.',re:'gain some breathing space'},
 {i:19,ru:'Местные повара были в авангарде развития фестиваля.',en:'Local chefs were at the forefront of the festival’s development.',note:'Keep at the forefront of together. Change be to fit the subject and time.',re:'(were|was|are|is|be) at the forefront of'}
],
use:[
 {q:'Tell about a local event that changed while it was underway. What went wrong, who helped, and how did it end?',chunks:[['in full swing','in full swing'],['contend with','contend(s|ed|ing)? with'],['pull sb through','pull(s|ed|ing)? .{0,45} through'],['cap sth off with','cap(s|ped|ping)? .{0,45} off(?: .{0,45})? with']],model:'Our neighborhood book fair was in full swing when a storm knocked out the power. We had to contend with dark halls, wet books, and a confused schedule. At first, visitors simply waited and checked their phones, but volunteers pulled us through by moving every table into the courtyard. Local authors continued their readings under a covered walkway, and children helped dry the display boards. The organizers capped the afternoon off with an outdoor reading just as the sun returned. Although the storm changed our plans, it also made the event feel more cooperative and memorable.'},
 {q:'Describe a group project that succeeded despite confusion. What did people worry about, and how was the dispute settled?',chunks:[['fret over','fret(s|ted|ting)? over'],['divide and conquer','divide and conquer'],['fight it out','fight(s)? it out|fought it out'],['gain some breathing space','gain(s|ed|ing)? some breathing space']],model:'On one group project, I fretted over every small detail instead of listening to other people. Nobody benefited when one member privately tried to divide and conquer the team by forming separate chats. Eventually, the rest of us fought it out over the schedule in one direct meeting rather than exchanging irritated messages. Extending the deadline gained some breathing space, so we could test our work properly. The final result improved, but the more useful lesson was about trust: clear roles and one shared conversation prevented the same confusion from returning.'},
 {q:'Talk about a small tradition that began by accident. How did it develop, and did anyone plan that growth?',chunks:[['the germ of sth','the germ of'],['throwaway gesture','throwaway gestures?'],['blossom into','blossom(s|ed|ing)? into'],['take its natural course','take(s|n|ing)? (its|their) natural course|took (its|their) natural course']],model:'The germ of our family picnic was a throwaway gesture: my uncle unexpectedly placed a blanket in the garden after Sunday lunch. We enjoyed the afternoon so much that we repeated it the following month. That small action gradually blossomed into an annual gathering with homemade food and old photographs. Nobody imposed a program; we let the tradition take its natural course. Now everyone contributes something, but the day still feels informal. I like that its origin was accidental, because nobody feels responsible for preserving an elaborate or artificial ritual.'},